      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Bryan.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 3, power rating 100 → a level 3 Cleric player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 3 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Toad God's Instrument of Judgment, Currently Lost in the Shadowfell</strong> — Servant of the Toad God / Affiliated with Mystic Morel's hunting party</p><p>Status: Active — last confirmed location: the Shadowfell grove, where a massive fireball was hurled at Mazebounds</p><p>Bryan is the servant of a deity he calls the Toad God, and he arrived at Raventree's extended crisis with the mission-oriented certainty of someone who has received divine instruction and the practical limitations of someone who has never actually been to the Shadowfell. He recruited Dan from the Mages' Guild barracks, partnered with Mystic Morel for planar transit, and entered the Shadowfell hunting Archie Miser under a theological mandate that he described as being 'for the good of the world.' He found the Mazehound grove instead. A massive fireball was hurled. Waluigi does not know whose fireball it was or whether Bryan survived the grove encounter. Waluigi notes that anyone hunting Archie Miser in the Shadowfell while carrying a mandate from a Toad God and traveling with a fortune-telling pickpocket is operating at a significant information disadvantage relative to the situation they have entered. WAH.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Instrument of Judgment</strong> — “The Toad God's Instrument of Judgment, Currently Lost in the Shadowfell”</li><li><strong>Toad God's Mandate</strong> — “Bryan is the servant of a deity he calls the Toad God, and he arrived at Raventree's extended crisis with the mission-oriented certainty of someone who has received divine instruction and the practical limitations of”</li><li><strong>Divine Judgment</strong> — “A sincere Toad God servant who reaches Archie and believes divine judgment demands action will act.”</li><li><strong>Power Rating 100</strong> — “The Toad God's Instrument of Judgment, Currently Lost in the Shadowfell”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/bryan</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/bryan</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
